oxed - SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION
Document: OXED-SRS-001
Revision: 0.2-draft
Status: DRAFT
Date: 2026-11-20

1. SCOPE

1.1 oxed is an ed-first terminal editor written in OxCaml.
1.2 Keyboard, mouse, ed, and LSP edits share one transaction engine.
1.3 Visual features augment, rather than replace, command composition.

2. CONVENTIONS

2.1 MUST, SHOULD, and MAY follow RFC 2119 and RFC 8174.
2.2 Each REQ identifier is unique and remains stable across revisions.
2.3 Every MUST requirement requires verification evidence.

3. ARCHITECTURE

3.1 Main       Application lifecycle and resource cleanup
3.2 App        Event routing, dispatch, and rendering
3.3 Terminal   Lambda-term input, display, and mouse
3.4 Workspace  Files, buffers, and active document
3.5 Editor     Zed-backed text, cursors, selections, and undo
3.6 Ed         Addressing and command interpretation
3.7 Syntax     Tree-sitter parsing and syntax overlays
3.8 Language   LSP processes and language services

4. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

REQ-001 Editor MUST own authoritative text and cursor state.
REQ-002 All editing inputs MUST use a common transaction pathway.
REQ-003 Ed MUST support ., $, numbers, marks, searches, and ranges.
REQ-004 Ed MUST support p, a, i, c, d, s, g, w, q, and u.
REQ-005 An @ selection address MAY extend traditional ed syntax.
REQ-006 Workspace MUST support opening, editing, and saving files.
REQ-007 Terminal MUST support keyboard, mouse, and resizing.
REQ-008 Terminal MUST restore its state after normal termination
        and recoverable failures.
REQ-009 Syntax MUST maintain an incremental, derived parse tree.
REQ-010 Language MUST support versioned LSP document state.
REQ-011 Stale LSP results MUST NOT overwrite newer text state.
REQ-012 Position conversion MUST handle Unicode scalar positions,
        UTF-8 byte offsets, and LSP UTF-16 offsets.
REQ-013 File operations MUST preserve buffer integrity on failure.
REQ-014 Release builds MUST NOT contain reachable TODO stubs.

5. IMPLEMENTATION CONSTRAINTS

5.1 OxCaml with Base, Core, and Core_unix.
5.2 Zed provides Unicode editing and rope infrastructure.
5.3 Lambda-term provides terminal interaction.
5.4 Lwt coordinates asynchronous operations.
5.5 Tree-sitter provides incremental syntax analysis.
5.6 LSP protocol types and process transport remain separate.
5.7 Zed refers to the OCaml library, not the Rust Zed editor.

6. VERIFICATION

VER-001 Native compilation and interface compatibility.
VER-002 Terminal acquisition, restoration, and repeated cleanup.
VER-003 File open, edit, save, and reopen round trips.
VER-004 Ed command, address, and undo regression tests.
VER-005 Keyboard, mouse, scrolling, and resize tests.
VER-006 Incremental syntax parsing and highlighting tests.
VER-007 LSP synchronization and stale-response tests.
VER-008 Unicode position-conversion round-trip tests.
VER-009 Exception, crash, and partial-write recovery tests.

7. CURRENT STATUS

7.1 Application skeleton compiles.
7.2 VER-002 passed for normal exit, injected exception, and
    repeated close.
7.3 Remaining verification items are pending.

8. OPEN DECISIONS

8.1 App event representation and multiplexing.
